Real world applications 1: 🎓 Student Record File System

📌 Brief Description

The Student Record File System is a C++ program that stores student information such as roll number, name, and marks in a CSV-like text file.

The program demonstrates how to write student records into a file, read the records back, parse the stored data, and display a student report.

🔑 Key Concepts

- 📄 Text-file handling
- ✍️ "ofstream" for writing
- 📖 "ifstream" for reading
- 🔍 "getline()" for parsing
- 🛡️ File-open validation
- 🏫 Class-based record management

🌍 Real-World Application

This concept can be used in college management systems, examination systems, student databases, and academic record management.

🎯 Main Purpose

To demonstrate how student data can be stored permanently in a file and retrieved whenever required.
